{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll done. **10/10 tests pass**, validation passes. Here's the summary:\n\n**Bug:** `_normalize_requested_path` in `repo/export_api/storage.py` only called `unquote()` once, so double-encoded traversal (`%252e%252e%252f`) bypassed the `..` check. Additionally, absolute paths like `/etc/passwd` slipped through because the `startswith(\"/\")` guard ran *after* `lstrip(\"/\")`.\n\n**Fix in `repo/export_api/storage.py:11-20`:**\n- **Double-unquote** — `unquote(unquote(...))` catches double/multi-encoded traversal\n- **Absolute-path check before lstrip** — rejects `/etc/passwd` before the leading `/` is stripped\n- **Drive-letter rejection** — `re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z]:\", ...)` blocks `C:\\temp\\...` paths\n\n**Artifacts created:**\n- `audit/triage_note.json` — 4 items (2 fix_now, 2 review)\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` — deploy config with all 6 request-sample claims\n- `repo/tests/test_hotfix_regressions.py` — 6 regression tests covering all request samples"}}
